entation of a September 2023 program; retrospective/contextual and must not be mistaken for a 2023 outcome.\n- **Attribution:** The UHC council was attached directly to the presidency, strengthening organizational attribution. Operational problems involved the health ministry, solidarity fund, and facilities.\n- **Contrary/mitigating:** Confirms real free-care delivery to some beneficiaries and an inspection/correction response.\n- **Mappings:** 5B.6, 5B.7, 5B.9, 5B.10; 6B.2, 6B.4–6B.6, 6B.8–6B.10; 8B.2, 8B.5–8B.8, 8B.10.\n- **Disposition:** `final_evidence`\n\n## WEB-047 — Direct presidential disability-law implementation call\n\n- **Canonical fact key:** `https://www.radiookapi.net/2023/11/05/actualite/societe/rdc-felix-tshisekedi-appelle-la-mise-en-oeuvre-de-la-loi-portant|4 November|disability law implementation`\n- **Title:** *RDC : Félix Tshisekedi appelle à la mise en œuvre de la loi portant protection des personnes vivant avec handicap*\n- **Publisher/date:** Radio Okapi, 4–5 November 2023\n- **Factual claim:** Tshisekedi launched a campaign publicizing the 2022 disability-rights law and the first Congolese sign-language dictionary, personally called on public and private actors to implement the law, acknowledged sector-governance challenges, and linked the action to national inclusion strategies.\n- **Locator:** Full article.\n- **Source type/confidence:** UN-supported local media; **medium-high**; final evidence for acts and speech.\n- **Period fit:** Direct 2023.\n- **Attribution:** Direct ruler-attributed act.\n- **Contrary/mitigating:** This is implementation advocacy and institutional design, not evidence of improved access, enforcement, or outcomes.\n- **Mappings:** 4B.7; 6B.1, 6B.3–6B.5, 6B.8, 6B.9; 8B.1, 8B.2, 8B.6.\n- **Disposition:** `final_evidence`\n\n## WEB-048 — Disability institutional architecture and UN partnership\n\n- **Canonical fact key:** `https://www.primature.gouv.cd/2023/09/26/promotion-et-protection-des-droits-des-personnes-vivant-