e the fetched excerpt.\n- **Source type/confidence:** Foreign-government country assessment; **medium-high** for institutional risk; final/context evidence.\n- **Period fit:** Direct 2023.\n- **Attribution:** Country and administration environment only; not proof of personal misconduct by Tshisekedi.\n- **Contrary/mitigating:** It notes anti-corruption frameworks and tighter extractive-industry regulation, though implementation was weak.\n- **Mappings:** 4B.2, 4B.4, 4B.10; 5B.4, 5B.5; 7B.3, 7B.5–7B.7, 7B.9, 7B.10; 8B.5, 8B.7.\n- **Disposition:** `context`\n\n## WEB-050 — Cabinet reshuffle served electoral coalition and security strategy\n\n- **Canonical fact key:** `https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2023/3/24/congo-president-tshisekedi-brings-in-former-vp-bemba-in-reshuffle-ahead-of-election|24 March reshuffle|Bemba Kamerhe Mbusa appointments`\n- **Title:** *DRC’s President Tshisekedi Reshuffles Cabinet Ahead of Election*\n- **Publisher/date:** Al Jazeera, 24 March 2023\n- **Factual claim:** Search discovery reported that Tshisekedi appointed Jean-Pierre Bemba as defence minister and brought Vital Kamerhe and Antipas Mbusa Nyamwisi into senior roles before the election.\n- **Locator:** Underlying page could not be fetched.\n- **Source type/confidence:** Reputable media if opened; currently gateway-only.\n- **Period fit:** Direct 2023.\n- **Attribution:** Direct appointment authority.\n- **Mappings:** Potential 2B.3, 2B.5; 5B.2; 7B.5, 7B.9; 8B.3–8B.5, 8B.9.\n- **Disposition:** `discovery_only`\n- **Reason:** `underlying_source_unavailable_connection_failure`\n- **Research gap:** A precise opened source is still needed before using the reshuffle as evidence of competence, coalition management, patronage, or security direction.\n\n---\n\n# New rejected or disposition-changed candidates\n\nThese entries should be added to the manifest even though they are not retained as evidence.\n\n1. **UN Group of Experts S/2024/432**\n   - URL: `https://digitallibrary.un.org/record/405