eated as realized outcomes.\n- Later family allegations and 2025–26 achievement pages remain excluded.\n\n### Remaining gaps\n\n- Budget execution across the full program portfolio.\n- Opened IMF outcome tables.\n- Exact cabinet/interagency coordination chains.\n- Independent education learning outcomes.\n- Longer-run durability without silently expanding the period.\n- Primary evidence distinguishing presidential management from ministerial and donor initiative.\n\n### Saturation assessment\n\nThe reviewer asked for targeted execution and outcome evidence rather than generic achievements. That was materially achieved for the state of siege, Goma response, PDL-145T, maternity care, CENI appointments, and disability policy. Remaining gaps require inaccessible primary documents or post-period outcomes that cannot be imported wholesale into 2023.\n\n---\n\n# Round-1 manifest accounting\n\n## Add as `final_evidence`\n\n`WEB-027`, `WEB-028`, `WEB-029`, `WEB-030`, `WEB-031`, `WEB-032`, `WEB-033`, `WEB-034`, `WEB-036`, `WEB-037`, `WEB-038`, `WEB-039`, `WEB-040`, `WEB-042`, `WEB-045`, `WEB-046`, `WEB-047`\n\n## Add as `context`\n\n`WEB-035`, `WEB-041`, `WEB-044`, `WEB-048`, `WEB-049`\n\n## Add as `discovery_only`\n\n`WEB-043`, `WEB-050`, UN S/2024/432, CENCO-ECC final PDF, State Department 2023 Human Rights PDF, IMF 2024/226 PDF/release, World Bank poverty brief\n\n## Add as `rejected`\n\nUN N23/364/37 blocked PDF, AU observer image PDF, CENCO-ECC preliminary raw PDF, Tsieleka IGF page, later family allegations, unsuccessful 2023 asset-declaration and false-statement candidates\n\n## Changed disposition\n\n- **International Crisis Group Goma Q&A:** initial `rejected` → `final_evidence` as `WEB-032`.\n- **EU observation inference:** WEB-009 remains final evidence for cancellation, but its narrative must be amended with WEB-038 so the equipment issue is not characterized as proven deliberate obstruction.\n\n---\n\n# Round-1 global self-audit\n\n## Attribution improvements\n\nDirect ruler-attributed evidence now exists for:\n\n- creating and continuing the state of siege;\n- appointing military/police authorities under it;\n- ordering investigation and sanctions after Goma;\n- partially easing emergency rule;\n- formally appointing the contested CENI leadership;\n- launching maternity coverage;\n- calling for disability-law implementation.\n\n## Attribution limits preserved\n\nNo evidence established that Tshisekedi:\n\n- ordered the Goma massacre;\n- personally directed CENI irregularities;\n- personally diverted PDL funds;\n- personally profited from office in 2023;\n- knowingly made a specific false statement;\n- knew of particular allied-militia atrocities before enabling further support.\n\n## Strongest new contrary evidence\n\n- Tshisekedi acted promptly after notification of Goma.\n- Soldiers were prosecuted and convicted.\n- Emergency restrictions were partly eased.\n- Domestic observers found a clear presidential leader despite irregularities.\n- EU observation failure had plausible technical/security causes.\n- Maternity care reached at least some intended beneficiaries.\n- PDL-145T remained potentially valuable despite severe execution failures.\n- Disability institutions and policy architecture were created, though outcomes were unproved.\n\n## Source concentration\n\nThe round added multiple Radio Okapi items, but each concerns a distinct event or official act. They are one organization, not multiple independent source families. The PDL items share the same CREFDL underlying investigation; WEB-041 is only corroborating publication, not a new source family.\n\n## Overall continuation result\n\nRound 1 materially improved Chapters **3B, 4B, 5B, 6B, and 8B**. It modestly improved **2B** through formal security-policy attribution. It did not solve the core personal-nexus problem in **7B**, despite targeted adverse and exculpatory searches. No score, score range, anchor, or ranking recommendation was produced."}}
